<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $3.1 mln Sept 20.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $3.1 mln Sept 20.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $3.1 million surplus on Sept 20 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 20</p>
<p>Exports: $193.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $165.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $135.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $159.7 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $3.1 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.191 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.426 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.241 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.775 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $231 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
